### MODEL (turn 4)
The bug was in `parse_amount` in `ledger/money.py`: a one-digit fraction was read as cents directly, so `10.5` became 1005 cents instead of 1050. The fraction is now padded to two digits before conversion, and I added assertions for `10.5`, `10.`, and `10` to `tests/test_ledger.py`. All three tests pass.
